I hoisted the profile pointer into a local and added branch-prediction hints so the common non-null, in-range path stays as fall-through. This reduces redundant loads and keeps the hot path branch-efficient.

```cpp
FIT_FLOAT64 Field::GetOffset() const
{
    const Profile* p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect(p == NULL, 0))
        return 0;
    if (__builtin_expect(profileIndex >= p->numFields, 0))
        return 0;
    return p->fields[profileIndex].offset;
}
```